# The proposals site must not rank at all (Will, 2026-09-22). Organic search
# belongs to www.getshortcut.co; CLE ranks from /solutions/law-firms there.
#
# One rule for every path, including the SPA shell served at every route and
# the static files (images, PDFs, markdown) Netlify serves directly. Headers in
# this file match the REQUEST path, so the /* -> /index.html rewrite in
# netlify.toml does not strip it (verified 2026-09-22 against the old
# /holiday-page/* rule, which showed on a path that only exists as a rewrite).
#
# noindex, not a robots.txt Disallow: Google has to be able to crawl a page to
# see this header, and a Disallowed URL can stay in the index as "Indexed,
# though blocked by robots.txt". robots.txt therefore stays Allow: /.
#
# Plain noindex, not nofollow: links from here to www should still count.
#
# This replaced a /holiday-page/* "index, follow" rule, which would have been
# merged with this one into contradictory directives. Do not add per-path
# "index" rules below; there is no page on this site that should rank.
/*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex

# Cache control for static assets
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  
/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  
/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable


